1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
A signer signs whatever bytes it is given.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Solana Keychain gives one signing
interface across many backends,

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
and leaves transaction checks to you.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Signing Firewall sits
in front of the signer.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
It decodes the transaction,
checks it against a policy,

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
and lets the signer sign what passes.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Legacy, v0 with a lookup table,
the new v1 format, and a P-Token batch.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Each one passes and lands on devnet.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Above two USDC, a second person approves.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The approval covers these exact bytes.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Change the amount after approval: blocked.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Pay into a token account
someone else owns: blocked.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Split an amount over the cap
into three transfers: blocked.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Hide a delegate approval
inside a batch: blocked.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Use a durable nonce: blocked.

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Put a fee in the v1 config that
an instruction scan would miss: blocked.

17
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
The signer was never called.

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
An AI agent pays for an API with x402.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
It pays the quote it accepted,
byte for byte, and nothing else.

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
A hostile shop offers four bad options.

21
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,000
The SDK's own cap limits only the amount,
so the payee, the token

22
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
and the fee payer are the guard's job:
all blocked before signing.

23
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Over the daily budget: blocked.

24
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
On the other side,
a facilitator refuses a payment

25
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,300
that only approves a delegate
instead of moving tokens.

26
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,000
The public test vectors can be run

27
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
by any wallet or x402
implementation.

28
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:20,000
And every message that landed
matches the bytes that were reviewed.

29
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Open source under Apache 2.0.
Built in Tokyo by NexBridge.
